# Expected:
# 5
# 6

# A `comptime` binding is a constant: reassigning it used to be accepted, silently turning
# the constant into a runtime variable (the checker never looked at the mark). It is now
# refused with "Cannot assign to 'N'; a `comptime` binding is a constant".
comptime N = 5;
write(N);

# An ordinary variable is still reassignable — and the same name in ANOTHER scope is
# another variable: the protection is per scope, not per name (a name-keyed global set
# refused the `i` counters of the prelude functions because of a `comptime for i`).
x = 5;
x = 6;
write(x);
